---
<section class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 1rem;">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">engagement models</span>
    <h1 style="max-width: 16ch;">Three ways to work with us<span class="hero__cursor"></span></h1>
    <p class="hero__sub">Exact numbers depend on scope — this page is about the shape of the engagement, not a locked price list. We'll give you real numbers after the discovery call.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-border-top">
  <div class="container grid grid-3 reveal">
    <div class="price-card">
      <div class="price-card__model">Fixed scope</div>
      <h3 style="font-size: var(--step1);">Project-based</h3>
      <p>Best for a defined deliverable — a new site, a specific feature, a migration — with a clear start and finish.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Fixed price, agreed upfront</li>
        <li>Defined milestones & timeline</li>
        <li>Ideal for one-time builds</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card price-card--featured">
      <div class="price-card__model">Retainer</div>
      <h3 style="font-size: var(--step1);">Ongoing partnership</h3>
      <p>Best when you need continuous work across build, marketing, and support — this is where the dedicated-assistant model lives.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Monthly commitment, predictable cost</li>
        <li>Dedicated point of contact included</li>
        <li>Covers small requests without new quotes</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card">
      <div class="price-card__model">Staff augmentation</div>
      <h3 style="font-size: var(--step1);">Embedded support</h3>
      <p>Best when you have internal teams but need specialized capacity — ServiceNow expertise, for example — folded into your existing process.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Works inside your existing workflow</li>
        <li>Scoped by hours or by role</li>
        <li>Flexible ramp up or down</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-border-top">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="callout reveal">
      <div class="callout__icon">$</div>
      <div>
        <h3>No surprise invoices.</h3>
        <p>Whichever model fits, scope boundaries are agreed upfront. If a request grows beyond what's covered, we flag it clearly before any additional cost — never after.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-border-top text-center">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 style="max-width: 20ch; margin: 0 auto 1rem;">Not sure which model fits?</h2>
    <p class="mx-auto max-w" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Tell us about the project and we'll recommend the right structure — no pressure to commit to more than you need.</p>
    <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Start a project →</a>
  </div>
</section>
